      "technical_explanation": "The flagged module is a static data file exporting an array of default preset objects: display names, pass identifiers, enable flags, context lengths, plain-language prompt templates, empty connection strings, and toggles for injecting character, world-info, and scene context into each pass. There are no encoded or packed literals, no dynamic evaluation, no hidden second-stage payloads, no network destinations, and no credential or host-state access. The content directly matches the extension's stated purpose of shipping editable default post-processing passes. The obfuscation signal is a false positive, most plausibly triggered by the long multi-line template literals, emoji, and XML-style markup embedded in the prompt text; the scanner itself reported low confidence and retained no matched literals, so the candidate-locating signal is not supported by the actual code.",
